// Title: User Has Been Deleted Via Userdel
// Sigma ID: 08f26069-6f80-474b-8d1f-d971c6fedea0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Tuan Le (NCSGroup)
// Date: 2022-12-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1531
// Description: Detects execution of the "userdel" binary. Which is used to delete a user account and related
//   files. This is sometimes abused by threat actors in order to cover their tracks
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrator activities
// References:
//   - https://linuxize.com/post/how-to-delete-group-in-linux/
//   - https://www.cyberciti.biz/faq/linux-remove-user-command/
//   - https://www.cybrary.it/blog/0p3n/linux-commands-used-attackers/
//   - https://linux.die.net/man/8/userdel
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_userdel.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/userdel"
